            <ArticleTitle>The Science Behind Wear Testing for Great Toe Implants for Hallux Rigidus.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>891-902</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1083-7515(16)30047-X</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.fcl.2016.07.004</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Various methods of repairing damaged articular cartilage surfaces have been proposed and a variety of implant materials have been tried in an attempt to decrease pain and improve function after cartilage repair. The hydrogel made of polyvinyl alcohol and saline is a unique material used as an implant in the great toe for advanced stage arthritis.</AbstractText>
